{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Attendance",
    "description": "Two doors \u2014 the card scan at the gate and the manual fallback \u2014 plus the corrections. PATCH with a new employee_id RE-ALLOCATES the day and moves that day's production events with it.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Add Daily Worker",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/daily-workers",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "daily-workers"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Onboard a daily-wage worker on the floor. No login is created any more \u2014\nthe worker gets an employee record and a printable card, nothing else. Stays\nat DM/HR/MD (NOT widened to SUPERVISOR): adding people to the payroll is a\ndeliberate authority. The service gate is aligned to match.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"designation\": \"\",\n  \"phone\": \"\",\n  \"daily_rate\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Check In",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/check-in",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "check-in"
          ]
        },
        "description": "An OPERATOR records their own arrival (their login is linked to an\nemployee row). Workers never reach this \u2014 they have no login.\n\nThe body is OPTIONAL: with the geofence removed there is nothing to send.\n`{}`, `{\"lat\": .., \"lon\": ..}` (ignored) and no body at all all work.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"lat\": 0,\n  \"lon\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Check Out",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/check-out",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "check-out"
          ]
        },
        "description": "An OPERATOR records their own departure. Body optional \u2014 see check_in.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"lat\": 0,\n  \"lon\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Correct Attendance",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/{{attendance_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "{{attendance_id}}"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "attendance_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Fix a punch, or re-allocate it to the worker who was actually here.\n\nSending a different `employee_id` moves that day's production events too, in\nthe same transaction \u2014 otherwise attendance would say one name while the\ncutting log paid another, and wages are computed from the events.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"employee_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"check_in_at\": \"2026-08-01T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"check_out_at\": \"2026-08-01T09:00:00Z\",\n  \"reason\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Delete Attendance",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/{{attendance_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "{{attendance_id}}"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "reason",
              "value": "",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "attendance_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Remove a punch that should never have been made. `reason` is required.\n\nRefused (409) when the worker has production events that day: the work was\nreally done, so the cause is almost certainly a swapped card and the right\nfix is to re-allocate rather than delete."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "History",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/history",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "history"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "2026-08-01",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "end",
              "value": "2026-08-01",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "employee_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Attendance history for one employee.\n\nF36: only operators / floor leads may read a worker's history; CLIENT and\nVIEWER cannot reach it. (The self-service branch is gone with the employee\nlogin \u2014 a worker's own history is read by whoever is helping them, and\n/attendance/me still serves a staff login's own record.)"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "My History",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/me",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "me"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "2026-08-01",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "end",
              "value": "2026-08-01",
              "description": "",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": ""
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Proxy Check In",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/proxy/check-in",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "proxy",
            "check-in"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Manual check-in fallback for one or more employees (card failed / forgotten).\nSECURITY / HR / MD / DM. Works for ANY wage type. Only `employee_ids` is\nrequired \u2014 the operator's position is no longer asked for.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"employee_ids\": [\n    \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"\n  ],\n  \"lat\": 0,\n  \"lon\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Proxy Check Out",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/proxy/check-out",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "proxy",
            "check-out"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Manual check-out fallback. Same four operators, any wage type.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"employee_ids\": [\n    \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"\n  ],\n  \"lat\": 0,\n  \"lon\": 0\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Scan Check In",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/scan-check-in",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "scan-check-in"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Check in/out by scanning an employee barcode (direction = \"in\" | \"out\").\n\nNo position is requested or stored \u2014 `lat`/`lon` are accepted and ignored.\n\nTHE primary attendance door. Every employee has a card and no employee has a\nlogin, so the operator standing at the gate \u2014 SECURITY / HR / MD / DM \u2014 scans\nevery card, monthly or daily, including their own colleagues'.\n`proxy=True` marks the MANUAL fallback (card won't scan / forgotten).",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"employee_barcode\": \"\",\n  \"direction\": \"\",\n  \"lat\": 0,\n  \"lon\": 0,\n  \"proxy\": false\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Today Roster",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/attendance/today",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "attendance",
            "today"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Whole-floor roster. Operators + floor leads only."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ]
}